> I'm using a Slackware package of Qt Nethack that I found on
> LinuxPackages.net and I can't get my settings to save across exits,
> for the regular nethack options or the QT settings. There doesn't seem
> to be a .nethackrc defining settings in my home directory or
> in /usr/games/lib/nethackdir. Does anyone know how to store the
> settings?

You can't save all settings from your current game (though the game does
save some settings; I can't find where I left the message detailing
which).

You can write your own .nethackrc in your home directory, however. It
has to contain OPTIONS= lines; what OPTIONS are available is in the
Guidebook. You do have a Guidebook, don't you?

Obviously, only those settings you want different from the default have
to be in the .nethackrc, but it's often easier to put in what you want
without having to look up what is the default.

If you're still stuck, you're invited to email me privately and get an
annotated copy of my .nethackrc to tweak to your preferences. 

